like the Hachamat Lub and Professor Lieberman,

c0361
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:10.000
that special kind of admiration.

c0362
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.000
And it's the first time they met, right?

c0363
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.000
First and last.

c0364
00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.000
But what is very interesting,

c0365
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.000
is that even 20 years after,

c0366
00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:21.000
Professor Finkelstein and Professor Lieberman,

c0367
00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:23.000
Professor Lieberman,

c0368
00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.000
they will never forget that.

c0369
00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.000
Yes, yes.

c0370
00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.000
Because there is a, unfortunately,

c0371
00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:33.000
there is a lot of disinformation

c0372
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
in some circles,

c0373
00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:42.000
assuming that every Sepharadi Rabbi is an idiot.

c0374
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Well, in many cases they are right,

c0375
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.000
but Hachamat Lub al-Abadi was from the old school,

c0376
00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.000
through Tommy Hakham,

c0377
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:54.000
and they never met him.

c0378
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:59.000
There were some idiots parading in Israel

c0379
00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:05.000
as, you know, posing as so-called Sepharadi rabbis.

c0380
00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:08.000
But Hachamat Lub al-Abadi represents

c0381
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:11.000
a Sepharadi tradition that is vast.

c0382
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:16.000
Another person that I think is totally underrated,

c0383
00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:20.000
again, because we Sephardim are not particularly bright,

c0384
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:27.000
I think of him as the greatest pulpit Rabbi I ever met,

c0385
00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:31.000
was Rabbi David de Solopoul.

c0386
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.000
I consider him simply an outstanding Rabbi.

c0387
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.000
I mean, as the Rabbi's Rabbi.

c0388
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:42.000
I mean, the paradigm of how a Rabbi should function

c0389
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:48.000
in a modern synagogue.

c0390
00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.000
Did you meet him?

c0391
00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.000
Many times.

c0392
00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.000
And I not only met him,

c0393
00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:56.000
I was very fond of him,

c0394
00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.000
and he was the one who recommended me

c0395
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:05.000
to receive the postdoctorate fellowship at the seminary.

c0396
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Yes.

c0397
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:13.000
So I am particularly very fond of him.

c0398
00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
He was a great writer, of course.

c0399
00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:26.000
Sephardim are notorious for not appreciating Hachamat.

c0400
