c0413
00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:00.000
He was one of the wealthiest men in the community,

c0414
00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.000
not Hachamat Lub al-Abadi, another one.

c0415
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.000
And so we went,

c0416
00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:07.000
he wanted some money to help somebody,

c0417
00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.000
I don't remember the case.

c0418
00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:11.000
And then he told me something, Hachamat Lub al-Abadi,

c0419
00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.000
every time this man sees me,

c0420
00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:19.000
this terrible multi-millionaire,

c0421
00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:21.000
he shivers inside

c0422
00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:24.000
because he knows that I remember him

c0423
00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:26.000
when he was barefooted,

c0424
00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:28.000
walking barefooted in the streets.

c0425
00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:32.000
And I think that most people from the community

c0426
00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:35.000
shiver at Hachamat Lub al-Abadi.

c0427
00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:39.000
And they didn't want him to be al-Abadi,

c0428
00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.000
they preferred charlatans.

c0429
00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.000
And they got plenty of charlatans,

c0430
00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.000
and rabbis.

c0431
00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:49.000
But they didn't want Hachamat Lub al-Abadi,

c0432
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.000
because he knew.

c0433
00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:54.000
And since he was more or less well-off,

c0434
00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:57.000
they could not push him around.

c0435
00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:00.000
So they waited until he died.

c0436
00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:06.000
You put a book out to show them.

c0437
00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:10.000
Yes, but again, nobody reads it.

c0438
00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:18.000
It's just like having a Picasso exhibition

c0439
00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:22.000
in a Papuan village in New Guinea.

c0440
00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:30.000
Complete.

c0441
00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:38.000
Any...

c0442
00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:41.000
Actually, the library that the Knesset

c0443
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.000
were going today,

c0444
00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:45.000
I think he has a book there.

c0445
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.000
Of Hachamat Lub al-Abadi.

c0446
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:50.000
See, what is the important thing of the book?

c0447
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:53.000
The important thing of the book is

c0448
00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:57.000
that Hachamat Lub al-Abadi is the first

c0449
00:25:57.000 --> 00:26:00.000
and only Poseidon,

c0450
00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.000
whether Sepharadi or Ashkenaz,

c0451
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:05.000
to have to grace America.

c0452
00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:09.000
To have graced the shores of America.

c0453
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:12.000
Because this is a Pesah Kalachah.

c0454
00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:13.000
It has nothing to do with politics,

c0455
00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:15.000
it has nothing to do with theology.

c0456
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:17.000
With all due respect to Rabbi Moshe Feiglin,

c0457
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.000
we all cherish him.

c0458
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:21.000
The Pesahim are Pesahim by force,

c0459
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:23.000
by political force.

c0460
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.000
Without political force,

c0461
00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:29.000
the threat of violence,

c0462
00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.000
the Pesahim will not be accepted.

c0463
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.000
That is why I refuse to...

c0464
00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:39.000
I mean, sometimes I quote people,

c0465
00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:42.000
but I don't take them...

c0466
00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:45.000
I refuse to take them into...

c0467
00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:48.000
I would consider, for instance,

c0468
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:52.000
in my courses, Rabbi David Schluss.

c0469
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:55.000
Now, Rabbi David Schluss, nobody,

c0470
00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:56.000
or most people would not consider him

c0471
00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:59.000
as the greatest Pesahim of our time.

c0472
00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:01.000
But he has an advantage over other Pesahim

c0473
00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:03.000
that I know.

c0474
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:08.000
That his Teshuvot are not projected

c0475
00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:11.000
through political violence.

c0476
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:13.000
I go to his teshuba office,

c0477
00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:15.000
I say, oh, this is a great point.

c0478
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:16.000
Or I could ask questions,

c0479
00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:18.000
I don't agree, nothing,

c0480
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
there would be no violence.

c0481
00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:22.000
With the so-called,

c0482
00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:24.000
I don't consider them seriously,

c0483
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
the Pesahim in America,

c0484
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.000
